Phasmid: GPU identity in GPUInfo reports

What:     The GPU identity reported outside WebGL and WebGPU comes from gpu.*:
          webglcontextcreationerror.statusMessage (VENDOR, DEVICE, GL_VENDOR,
          GL_RENDERER, GL_VERSION), chrome://gpu (active GPU ids, strings,
          driver, GL_VENDOR, GL_RENDERER) and CDP SystemInfo.getInfo. Only
          the reports change: collection, blocklists, workarounds and the
          stored GPUInfo stay the host's. A field the claim does not
          determine is reported empty (id 0), never the host's.
Why:      The status message is page-visible and would name the host GPU next
          to the profile's WebGL renderer.
Profile:  gpu.vendor_id, device_id, vendor_name, device_name, driver_vendor,
          driver_version, gl_vendor, gl_renderer
Hooks:    content/renderer/renderer_blink_platform_impl.cc
          (CollectWebGLContextInfo); content/browser/gpu/gpu_internals_ui.cc
          (GetGpuInfo, GetGpuInfoDict);
          content/browser/devtools/protocol/system_info_handler.cc
          (SendGetInfoResponse); new content/browser/gpu/phasmid_gpu_info.{h,cc}
Contexts: main, cross-origin iframe and dedicated worker OffscreenCanvas
          (statusMessage); chrome://gpu and CDP (browser).
Guard:    tests/guards/graphics/gpu-info.py

